 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The selected center is disjoint from $U_Z$, hence its image in $X$ is\ndisjoint from $U$. A composite of finite-presentation closed immersions is\nfinite presentation, so the ambient center is finite presentation and its\nblow-up is $U$-admissible. By\n[lemma-nagata-strict-transform-ambient-closed], the strict transforms\nof $Z_1$ and $Z_2$ in this ambient blow-up agree with their strict\ntransforms in $\\operatorname{Bl}_C(Z)$, which are disjoint by the selected\npreparation witness.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-strict-transform-ambient-closed"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
